# Put this in ~/.mailcap, before the system one: its first text/html
# entry launches a browser, which is not what a terminal reader wants.

# w3m consults its own mailcap for a type it cannot render, so how
# markdown becomes HTML is said once, in ~/.w3m/mailcap, rather than
# twice. An entry there looks like:
#
#     text/markdown; pandoc -t html -f gfm %s; x-htmloutput
#
# Without one, put the conversion here instead:
#
#     text/markdown; pandoc -f gfm -t html %s | w3m -dump -T text/html -o display_borders=1; copiousoutput
text/markdown; w3m -dump -T text/markdown -o display_borders=1 -I %{charset} -O utf-8 %s; copiousoutput; description=Markdown text
text/html; w3m -dump -T text/html -I %{charset} -O utf-8 %s; copiousoutput; description=HTML text
application/mbox; cat %s; copiousoutput; description=patch series
